copyright holder is reinstated (a) provisionally, unless and until the
copyright holder explicitly and finally terminates your license, and
(b) permanently, if the copyright holder fails to notify you of the
termination by reasonable means prior to 60 days after the cessation.

Moreover, your license from a particular copyright holder is
reinstated permanently if the copyright holder notifies you of the
termination by reasonable means, you cease all violation of this
License, and you cease all violation of this License prior to 60 days
after the termination.

Termination of your license under this section terminates the
licenses of any other parties who have received copies or rights from
you under this License. However, it does not terminate the licenses
of parties who have received copies or rights from you under other
licenses.

3. Protecting Users' Legal Rights From Anti-Circumvention Law.

No covered work shall be deemed part of an effective technological
measure under any applicable law fulfilling the requirements of
article 11 of the WIPO copyright treaty adopted on 20 June 1996, or
similar laws prohibiting or restricting circumvention of such
measures.

When you convey a covered work, you waive any legal power to
enforce anti-circumvention technological measures to the extent
such enforcement is exercised by the work's operators, and you
convey the work under conditions that protect the freedom of other
users to do so. You must not convey a covered work under conditions
that do not protect the freedom of users to use and modify the
work, including conditions that would prohibit them from doing so.

4. Conveying Verbatim Copies.

You may convey verbatim copies of the Program's source code as you
receive it, in any medium, provided that you conspicuously and
appropriately display on each copy an appropriate copyright notice;
keep intact all notices stating that this License and any
non-permissive terms apply to the code; keep intact all notices of
the absence of any warranty; and give all recipients a copy of this
License along with the Program.

You may charge any price or no price for each copy that you convey,
and you may provide support or warranty services for the copies you
convey. You may charge a fee for the service of conveying the
covered work.

5. Conveying Modified Source Versions.

You may convey a work based on the Program, or the modifications to
produce it from the Program, in the form of source code under the
terms of section 4, provided that you also meet all of these conditions:

a) The work must carry prominent notices stating that you modified
it, and giving a relevant date.

b) The work must carry prominent notices that it is released under
this License and any conditions imposed under section 10. This
condition modifies the requirement of section 4 to "keep intact all
notices".

c) You must license the entire work, as a whole, under this License
to anyone who comes into possession of a copy. This License will
therefore apply, along with any applicable section 10 conditions,
to the whole of the work.

d) If the work has interactive user interfaces, each must display
Appropriate Legal Notices; however, if the Program has interactive
user interfaces that do not display Appropriate Legal Notices, your
work is not required to make them do so.

6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this
License, in one of these ways:

a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by the
Corresponding Source fixed on a durable physical medium
(including a physical distribution medium) that accompanies the
product.

b) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a
written offer, valid for at least three years and valid for as
long as you offer spare parts or customer service for that product,
to give anyone who possesses the object code a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium (including a
physical distribution medium) or through a network accessible to
the public at no charge.

c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium (including a
physical distribution medium).

d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated
place (gratis or for a fee), and offer equivalent access to the
Corresponding Source in the same way through the same place at no
charge. If the designated place is a network server, the
Corresponding Source may be on a different server (operated by or
for the same operators) provided you specify the corresponding
server. This offers corresponds to offering a warranty for the
object code, but may not be applicable to all products.

e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer networks, provided
you inform other peers of the object code and the Corresponding
Source is made available in the same way.

A separable portion of the object code, whose source code is
excluded from the Corresponding Source as a System Library, need
not be accompanied by the Corresponding Source, provided you
clearly inform the recipients of the missing source and the offer
of the Corresponding Source applies only to the extent that the
excluded portion is not a System Library.

