11. Patents.

A "contributor" is a copyright holder who authorizes the use of
this License for the work. The "contributor's patent claims" are
the patent claims that the contributor directly controls, or that
are directly controlled by the contributor's organization. A
"contribution" is the copyrighted work of a contributor.

Each contributor grants you a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free
patent license under the contributor's patent claims, to make, use,
sell, offer for sale, import and otherwise run, modify and convey
the covered work, to the extent necessary to exercise the rights
granted by this License.

If you convey a covered work, and you knowingly rely on a patent
claim that is asserted by a third party against you or any recipient
of your covered work, and you make a claim that your covered work
satisfies the patent claim, the patent claim will be treated as a
contribution from that third party, and you will be required to
license your other patent claims under this License.

If a patent claim is asserted against you or any recipient of a
covered work, and you make a claim that your covered work satisfies
the patent claim, the patent claim will be treated as a contribution
from that third party, and you will be required to license your other
patent claims under this License.

